course: dictionary
lesson: 998
title: Boiling: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one the writer means. «The water in the pan was boiling.» Here boiling means so hot that it bubbles and turns into steam.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «It was a boiling hot day.» Nobody thinks the day is bubbling, so boiling means very hot. «He was boiling with anger» means he was very angry, so the word is not about water at all.
explain: Boil can also be a verb, an action word. «Boil the pasta for ten minutes» means heat the water until it bubbles. Always try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: «Boiling» describes a liquid that is so hot it bubbles and turns into steam.
fact: «Boiling» can also mean very hot, as in «a boiling hot day».
fact: Water boils at 100 °C (212 °F) at sea level. The boiling point is the temperature where a liquid turns into a gas.
fact: «The bubbles in boiling water are water vapour, not air.»
fact: Boiling water and a boiling kettle can burn your skin badly, so keep well away from the stove.
exercise: «The bubbles in boiling water are water vapour, not air.» What are the bubbles made of? | Sugar | Soap | *Water vapour | Air
exercise: «He was boiling with anger after the argument.» What does boiling mean here? | Covered in soap | *Very angry | Very cold | Bubbling in a pan
exercise: Mum says, «Bring the water to the boil, then add the pasta.» What does bring to the boil mean? | Put the lid on and let it go cold | Stir it slowly with a spoon | *Heat it until it bubbles | Pour the water away
test: «The white cloud above a boiling kettle is tiny drops of water.» What is the white cloud made of? | Dust from the kitchen | *Tiny drops of water | Gas you cannot see | Smoke from a fire
test: Which word means so hot that it bubbles and turns into steam? | Curt | Famished | Treacherous | *Boiling
exam: At what temperature does water boil at sea level? | 200 °C | *100 °C | 50 °C | 150 °C
